# Earth Rumble: the creature that fights is "up to one target creature you control", not necessarily the earthbent land. Bot1's
# Grizzly Bears fights Bot2's Elvish Mystic while the earthbent Forest stays out of it (no damage on it). The second target must be an
# opponent's creature: Bot1's own Bears and Forest are refused for it, and an opponent's creature is refused for the first (CR 603.12, 701.14a).

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Forest
Black Lotus
Grizzly Bears
Earth Rumble
Forest x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Elvish Mystic
Forest x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Grizzly Bears.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest#1.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Earth Rumble.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Forest#2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic)
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears)
! Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears)
! Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Forest#2)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears.Damage = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest#2.Types = Land; Creature
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest#2.Damage = 0
